Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-28-2000||01:13 AM||||My GT makes two distinct clicking noises. I know for a fact that one of them is the Manifold exhaust leak, but a couple of people have said it sounds like the injectors are making the other click.  I tend to agree, since it sounds like the the click is definitely coming from the manifold vicinity.  There's a guy here that works on Fiero's almost exclusively, and he thinks it's the injectors as well.  Is this somewhat normal?  The car runs fine.||||reg||1
Z||000001||sully5||03-28-2000||02:23 AM||||I have heard that this is normal for fuel injectors. At least that is what the service mgr at a Ford dealer told me about my f250. And he's my uncle, so i guess I can trust him!(sorry to mention the f-word). Have also heard a ticking on my Fiero, but being a newbie to this game and having a car that needs so much work it's hard for me to tell.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Standard||03-28-2000||04:54 AM||||On my 84 the TBI made quite a distinctive clicking noise.  Pretty loud.  You could hear it even with the air cleaner lid on and the decklid shut.  Can't hear the injectors on the V6, but the cracked front manifold kinda makes alotta noise.. but I guess you already knew that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Raydar||03-28-2000||01:07 PM||||GT Bastard... Yeah. They're pretty loud.<BR>When I bought my first GT in 85, I took it in for service because I thought all the lifters were clattering. Thought the same thing about my Formula a week ago, after I fixed a leaking Y-pipe. They'll fool ya'.   ||||reg||1
